    {
      "text": "Sableye lead quiet lives deep inside caverns. They are feared, however, because these Pokémon are thought to steal the spirits of people when their eyes burn with a sinister glow in the darkness.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sableye digs the ground with sharpened claws to find rocks that it eats. Substances in the eaten rocks crystallize and rise up to the Pokémon’s body surface.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It’s a fiend for gemstones, so it stalks Carbink. Unfortunately, Gabite almost always grabs them first.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon is feared. When its gemstone eyes begin to glow with a sinister shine, it’s believed that Sableye will steal people’s spirits away.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It digs through the ground with its hard claws and crunches down gems with its thick pointy teeth. Carbink is its favorite food.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Materials from gems it has eaten float to the surface of its body and can form an infinite number of patterns among individuals.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon is feared. When its gemstone eyes begin to glow with a sinister shine, it’s believed that Sableye will steal people’s spirits away.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "It feeds on gemstone crystals. In darkness, its eyes sparkle with the glitter of jewels.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
